public static int minPerfectSquareSum(int n) {
    if (n <= 0) return 0;

    int[] dp = new int[n + 1];
    for (int i = 0; i <= n; i++) {
        dp[i] = Integer.MAX_VALUE;
    }
    dp[0] = 0;

    for (int i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
        for (int j = 1; j <= (int)Math.sqrt(i); j++) {
            int perfectSquare = j * j;
            dp[i] = Math.min(dp[i], dp[i - perfectSquare] + 1);
        }
    }

    return dp[n];
}
```

The `minPerfectSquareSum` function initializes a dynamic programming array `dp` where `dp[i]` represents the minimum number of perfect square numbers that sum up to `i`. It iterates through each number `i` from 1 to `n`, and for each number, it checks every possible perfect square less than or equal to `i`. If a perfect square fits within the current range, it updates `dp[i]` by taking the minimum of its current value and `dp[i - perfectSquare] + 1`. Finally, the function returns the minimum number of perfect square numbers that sum up to `n`.

